			"type": "text",
			"text": "Golshanichthys was an arthrodire placoderm which lived in the Late Devonian of West Asia, first discovered near the city of Kerman in Iran around 1981. Its name means “Farrokh Golshani’s fish”, named after a member of the Geological Survery of Iran. It was a close relative of Dunkleosteus, either within the family Dunkleosteidae or the superfamily Dunkleosteoidea."
